Nicknamed "Igor" due to its slouched posture and massive hunchbacked frame, this suit sports a blue, silver, and white industrial paint scheme. Designed purely for power over agility, its hydraulic spine, reinforced legs, and heavy pneumatic pistons allow it to lift and hold tens of thousands of tons—serving as the design predecessor to the famous Hulkbuster armor.

In Iron Man 3, Mark XXXVIII delivers one of the most memorable moments during the House Party Protocol at the Norco oil rig: Tony commands Igor to prop up a massive collapsing loading crane platform, holding millions of pounds of steel in place so Tony and Rhodey can navigate the battle below safely.
